# Backend Rules (FastAPI)

## 1. Project structure
- routes/ → API endpoints
- services/ → business logic
- models/ → database models
- schemas/ → Pydantic DTOs
- core/ → config, settings

## 2. API design
- Always use Pydantic schemas for request/response
- Never return raw database models directly
- Use consistent response format:
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": ...,
    "message": ""
  }

## 3. Business logic
- Keep logic out of routes
- Put all logic in service layer
- Routes should only handle request/response

## 4. Error handling
- Use HTTPException for API errors
- Never return raw exceptions
- Standardize error messages

## 5. Database
- Use dependency injection for DB session
- Always close sessions properly
- Avoid raw SQL unless necessary

## 6. Code style
- Follow PEP8
- Use type hints everywhere
- Keep functions small and focused